Third-party material and dependencies
-------------------------------------

Mojo toolchain (Modular Inc.)
  mojo-dllm is written in Mojo and built with the `mojo` and `max-core`
  packages pinned in pixi.toml. The Mojo compiler and standard library source
  code is available under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions. The
  prebuilt conda/PyPI packages, including the runtime shared libraries a
  `mojo build` binary links against, are distributed under Modular's own
  license terms (LicenseRef-MAX-Platform-Software-License; see
  https://www.modular.com/legal). Anyone redistributing compiled mojo-dllm
  binaries must review those terms; this repository distributes source only.

llama.cpp (MIT, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors)
  scripts/gen_unicode_tables.py derives
  src/mojo_dllm/tokenizer/unicode_tables.mojo from llama.cpp's
  src/unicode-data.cpp, and the pre-tokenizer reproduces the `bailingmoe`
  regular expression from llama.cpp's src/llama-vocab.cpp.
  tools/ref/llada_ref.cpp links against libllama for testing only.

scripts/verify-action-pins.sh, scripts/action-pin-comments.py,
